  "consts": [
   "Parse the DESTINATION DETAILS section -> one OrderEntity per destination.\n\n        Only destination blocks under ``recipe.section_anchor`` are read, so the\n        earlier aggregate grid (and PACKAGING/COLOR DETAILS summaries) are ignored.\n\n        The PDF cycles colors inside the section (COLOR header -> per-destination\n        size blocks -> next color -> ...), so each destination's lines are scattered\n        across the document. We therefore accumulate ONE entity per destination CODE\n        (keyed dict), appending every color's inseam rows to that destination's buffer,\n        and only finalize all destinations at the end.\n\n        PDF ordering note: inside the section the COLOR header precedes its\n        ``Destination Code:`` line, and the per-destination ``Delivery Date:`` sits on\n        the FOLLOWING line. So colors/size-headers are captured whenever a color is\n        active, and the delivery date is attached to the current destination entity\n        when its own ``Delivery Date:`` line is seen. The inseam axis is kept on the\n        OrderLine so template_a can sum it into one color row.\n        ",
